Option 1: 
No-Code Tool (Quick Demo)
Tools: Chatbase, DocsBot, Poe (Knowledge Bases)

Steps: Upload PDF/Doc → Get chatbot link → Show demo.

✅ Easiest, no coding.

❌ Not much technical learning. Professors may feel it’s “too easy”.

 Option 2: 
Python + LangChain + ChromaDB 
Parse file → Split into text chunks.

Convert chunks into embeddings (OpenAI or HuggingFace).

Store embeddings in ChromaDB (free, works locally).

Build a chatbot UI using Streamlit or Gradio.

Ask questions → Retrieve relevant text → Pass into GPT (or open-source model).

👉 This shows understanding of AI pipelines and looks impressive in presentations.

Option 3: 
Open-Source Local LLM (Offline Project)
Use LLaMA 2 / Mistral + FAISS/ChromaDB.

Works without internet after setup.

Professors will like it because it looks fully custom.

Slightly heavier to run (needs a GPU or Colab).
